{"chunk_id": "bc242ed95523", "text": "On the tenth day of the Kurukshetra war, the armies of the Kauravas and Pandavas collide in a brutal struggle centered on Bhishma and Arjuna. The battlefield becomes a whirlpool of slaughter, the ground soaked with blood. Though riddled with arrows and still killing thousands, Bhishma finally faces Arjuna\u2019s relentless assault. Surrounded and pierced from every side, the grandsire is struck down and falls from his chariot just before sunset, yet his body remains suspended on a bed of arrows without touching the earth. Possessing the boon of choosing the moment of his death, he refuses to die during the inauspicious southern solstice and resolves to wait for the northern one. As sages in swan form witness his vow, both armies react with shock\u2014Pandavas rejoice, while the Kurus fall into grief and confusion\u2014marking a decisive turning point in the war.\nOn the tenth day, Arjuna fells Bhishma, who lies on a bed of arrows and chooses to delay death until the sun\u2019s northern solstice.\nThemes: fall of Bhishma, heroic sacrifice, fate and cosmic timing, battlefield devastation, control over death", "vector": [0.00418944051489234, -0.014149242080748081, -0.000517504580784589, 0.00578682916238904, -0.002481716452166438, 0.02866736613214016, -0.02507077157497406, 0.002328564878553152, -0.01956389658153057, -0.023041922599077225, 0.016085870563983917, 0.02122386358678341, -0.004861332010477781, 0.02018309012055397, 0.004364000633358955, -0.0021424773149192333, 0.03765226528048515, -0.008958552032709122, 0.025373781099915504, -0.017903929576277733, 0.0056814346462488174, -0.007318346295505762, -0.004278367385268211, 0.021500524133443832, -0.027455326169729233, 0.025215689092874527, 0.013819883577525616, -0.022053847089409828, 0.00664316164329648, -0.022976050153374672, -0.015282235108315945, 0.0006978283636271954, -0.01956389658153057, -0.005177516024559736, -0.038996048271656036, 0.00807587057352066, -0.0021243623923510313,